-- title:
--   Unit generation descends from a coefficient-field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a perfect field, let $K$ be a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure, let $F_k,F_K$ be the level-$25$ $q$-expansion function fields, and let $L_k⊆F_k$ and $L_K⊆F_K$ be the subfields generated by $U_0$ and $U_0/U_1$. If coefficient extension gives $L_K=F_K$, then already
--
--   $$L_k=F_k.$$
--
--   This descends modular-unit generation from a larger coefficient field to the original perfect field.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

